@page "/demo/versions"

<PageTitle>Versions — Blazor Reference</PageTitle>

<div class="demo-page">

  <GupContentHeader PageTitle="Versions">
    <PageSummary>What ships, where it comes from, and how it maps to the upstream design system.</PageSummary>
  </GupContentHeader>

  <div class="demo-body">

    <section class="demo-section">
      <p class="doc-lede">
        Unlike the upstream monorepo, which splits into separate component, token, icon,
        React and Angular packages, the Blazor port ships as a single NuGet package. The
        tokens, components and icon wiring all live in <code>GUPBlazor</code>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-section">
      <h2 class="demo-section-title">Package</h2>
      <div class="demo-surface">
        <table class="doc-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Package</th>
              <th scope="col">Version</th>
              <th scope="col">Target framework</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><code>GUPBlazor</code></th>
              <td>@Version</td>
              <td><code>net10.0</code></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        Published at
        <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/GUPBlazor" target="_blank" rel="noopener">nuget.org/packages/GUPBlazor</a>
        ·
        <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/GUPBlazor#versions-body-tab" target="_blank" rel="noopener">View all releases on NuGet.org</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-section">
      <h2 class="demo-section-title">Release History</h2>
      <div class="demo-surface">
        <table class="doc-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Version</th>
              <th scope="col">Highlights</th>
              <th scope="col">Status</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><code>0.3.1</code></th>
              <td>Scoped Storybook-style RTL component preview, live Arabic text switching, and CSS bidirectional fixes.</td>
              <td><strong>Latest</strong></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><code>0.3.0</code></th>
              <td>Upstream Storybook navigation mirroring, live design token alignment, and horizontal brand logo.</td>
              <td>Prior release</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><code>0.2.0</code></th>
              <td>Mobile responsive layout, touch target improvements, button group stacking, and interactive showcase.</td>
              <td>Prior release</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row"><code>0.1.0</code></th>
              <td>Initial release of core Gov.om Blazor components and design tokens on .NET 10.</td>
              <td>Initial milestone</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        For a complete log of all patch releases and package downloads, see the
        <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/GUPBlazor#versions-body-tab" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GUPBlazor Version History on NuGet.org</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-section">
      <h2 class="demo-section-title">Upstream reference</h2>
      <p>
        Component behaviour and design tokens are ported from the gov.om design system. The
        repository vendors a read-only snapshot of that source under
        <code>design-system/</code> as the porting reference.
      </p>
      <div class="demo-surface">
        <table class="doc-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Item</th>
              <th scope="col">Value</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Source</th>
              <td><a href="https://github.com/Gov-om/design-system" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/Gov-om/design-system</a></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">Live Storybook</th>
              <td><a href="https://storybook.service.gov.om/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">storybook.service.gov.om</a></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        The design tokens in this library are kept in step with the live design system
        rather than the vendored snapshot, which predates the current token naming.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="demo-section">
      <h2 class="demo-section-title">Versioning</h2>
      <p>
        The package follows semantic versioning while below <code>1.0.0</code>: the minor
        number moves for changes that alter rendered output or a component API, the patch
        number for fixes that do not. Pin an exact version if you need the visual output to
        stay fixed between upgrades.
      </p>
    </section>

  </div>
</div>

@code {
    private const string Version = "0.3.1";
}
